Kubernetes Deployment: Iron Gallery Application & MariaDB
📋 Overview
This project deploys a multi-tier web application consisting of the Iron Gallery frontend and a MariaDB database backend onto a Kubernetes cluster within a dedicated namespace (iron-namespace-xfusion).

The setup utilizes Deployments, Services (ClusterIP and NodePort), Persistent Volumes via emptyDir, and strict resource limits to ensure proper application containerization.

🏗️ Architecture & Component Specifications
1. Namespace
Name: iron-namespace-xfusion

2. Frontend: Iron Gallery Deployment & Service
Deployment Name: iron-gallery-deployment-xfusion

Namespace: iron-namespace-xfusion

Replicas: 1

Labels / Match Labels / Template Labels: run: iron-gallery

Container Name: iron-gallery-container-xfusion

Image: kodekloud/irongallery:2.0

Resource Limits:

CPU: 50m

Memory: 100Mi

Volumes & Mounts:

Config Volume (emptyDir) mounted at /usr/share/nginx/html/data

Images Volume (emptyDir) mounted at /usr/share/nginx/html/uploads

Service:

Name: iron-gallery-service-xfusion

Type: NodePort

Protocol: TCP

Port / TargetPort: 80

NodePort: 32678

3. Backend: Iron DB Deployment & Service
Deployment Name: iron-db-deployment-xfusion

Namespace: iron-namespace-xfusion

Replicas: 1

Labels / Match Labels / Template Labels: db: mariadb

Container Name: iron-db-container-xfusion

Image: kodekloud/irondb:2.0

Environment Variables:

MYSQL_DATABASE: database_blog

MYSQL_USER: db_user

MYSQL_PASSWORD: user_secure_pass123

MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: root_secure_pass123

Volume & Mount:

DB Volume (emptyDir) mounted at /var/lib/mysql

Service:

Name: iron-db-service-xfusion

Type: ClusterIP

Protocol: TCP

Port / TargetPort: 3306

⚙️ Kubernetes Manifest (iron-app.yaml)
YAML
apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: iron-namespace-xfusion
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: iron-gallery-deployment-xfusion
  namespace: iron-namespace-xfusion
  labels:
    run: iron-gallery
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      run: iron-gallery
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        run: iron-gallery
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: iron-gallery-container-xfusion
        image: kodekloud/irongallery:2.0
        resources:
          limits:
            memory: "100Mi"
            cpu: "50m"
        volumeMounts:
        - name: config
          mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html/data
        - name: images
          mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html/uploads
      volumes:
      - name: config
        emptyDir: {}
      - name: images
        emptyDir: {}
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: iron-db-deployment-xfusion
  namespace: iron-namespace-xfusion
  labels:
    db: mariadb
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      db: mariadb
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        db: mariadb
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: iron-db-container-xfusion
        image: kodekloud/irondb:2.0
        env:
        - name: MYSQL_DATABASE
          value: database_blog
        - name: MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD
          value: root_secure_pass123
        - name: MYSQL_USER
          value: db_user
        - name: MYSQL_PASSWORD
          value: user_secure_pass123
        volumeMounts:
        - name: db
          mountPath: /var/lib/mysql
      volumes:
      - name: db
        emptyDir: {}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: iron-db-service-xfusion
  namespace: iron-namespace-xfusion
spec:
  selector:
    db: mariadb
  ports:
  - protocol: TCP
    port: 3306
    targetPort: 3306
  type: ClusterIP
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: iron-gallery-service-xfusion
  namespace: iron-namespace-xfusion
spec:
  selector:
    run: iron-gallery
  ports:
  - protocol: TCP
    port: 80
    targetPort: 80
    nodePort: 32678
  type: NodePort
🚀 Deployment Instructions
Create and save the manifest file:

Bash
nano iron-app.yaml
(Paste the YAML configuration above, save, and exit)

Apply the configuration to the cluster:

Bash
kubectl apply -f iron-app.yaml
Verify the resources:

Bash
kubectl get all -n iron-namespace-xfusion
🔍 Validation & Preview
Pod Status Check: Ensure all pods transition to Running (1/1):

Bash
kubectl get pods -n iron-namespace-xfusion
Application Access: The frontend service is exposed externally on NodePort 32678, rendering the application installation and setup page successfully.
